WARNING: High Queue Latency Detected
====================================

The <%= @queue_name %> queue has high latency: <%= @latency.round %> seconds

This means jobs are taking too long to be picked up for processing.

POSSIBLE CAUSES:
- Too many jobs queued
- Not enough Sidekiq workers
- Long-running jobs blocking the queue
- Database or Redis performance issues

RECOMMENDED ACTIONS:
1. Check queue size and job types:
   $ bundle exec rails console -e production
   > queue = Sidekiq::Queue.new("<%= @queue_name %>")
   > queue.size
   > queue.first(10).map(&:klass)

2. Add more workers if needed:
   $ sudo systemctl start sidekiq-workers@4
   $ sudo systemctl start sidekiq-workers@5

3. Check for stuck jobs:
   > Sidekiq::Workers.new.each { |p, t, m| puts "#{m['queue']}: #{m['payload']['class']}" }

4. Monitor Redis performance:
   $ redis-cli --stat

5. Check system resources:
   $ top
   $ free -h
   $ df -h

